From ae7b26a7f0e420e97ef2d49a4ec775e5b938d7c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabe Ochoa <urgentcactus@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:13:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add bounded jobs, byte-budget cache, image decode and texture
 upload; watcher generations

- plugins/jobs.h: Executor with bounded foreground/background queues, a
  reserved foreground worker, explicit Rejected/Pending/Cancelled/Completed/
  Failed outcomes, shutdown that cancels reads and drains must-complete jobs,
  Generation tickets for stale completions, and BusyDelay.
- plugins/byte_budget_cache.h: LRU bounded by a host cost function with
  oversize rejection and hit/miss/eviction/rejection/byte stats.
- plugins/image_decode.{h,cpp}: limited, cancellable stb decode to owned
  RGBA8 with an optional shared Budget and structured errors.
- load_texture_from_rgba on raylib, sokol and none, returning nullopt on
  failure.
- file_watcher: Event::generation and Watcher::generation(); test covers
  generations and stop racing start under file churn.
- Tests registered in tests/makefile; docs/plugins.md, PLUGIN_API.md and
  CHANGELOG.md describe the contracts.
